'''Khari Sendo''' was a [[human]] member of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. As a [[youngling]] she was part of [[Majestic Aiwha Clan]], demonstrating early signs of leadership and encouraging her fellow students to share their feelings. In [[132 BBY]], she attended a class led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] where Sol had the students [[Meditation|meditate]] and connect with [[the Force]]. When he asked what they saw, Sendo stated she saw balance. Sol approved of her interpretation and soon dismissed the class for [[Foodstuff|lunch]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Connect to the Force. Have faith. Think of diving into a great ocean. Give yourselves over to its weight, its stillness, its uncertainty. And tell me what comes into your mind.|Sol instructs Sendo and her class|audio=Sol-ConnectToTheForce-LostFound.flac|<ref name="LostFound" />}}
[[File:SolTeaching-LostFound.png|thumb|right|300px|alt=Sol, wearing white and yellow temple robes, stands on a veranda in the Jedi Temple with a view over the Coruscant skyline. Seated arouned him on the floor are younglings including Khari Sendo, Xilawa Dater, Jev Eremia, Tenina Sha-Dand, and Chippin Jat.|Khari Sendo (center) was a Jedi youngling on Coruscant during the High Republic Era.]]
Khari Sendo was a [[human]] member of the [[Jedi Order]]'s [[Majestic Aiwha Clan]] as a [[youngling]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> she<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> was part of a class of [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] that was taught by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] on a training veranda in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. The master instructed Sendo and the other students to [[Meditation|meditate]] and close their [[eye]]s, telling them that their sight could be deceived and so should not be trusted.<ref name="LostFound" />

After Sol instructed the students to connect to [[the Force]] and tell him what entered their minds, there was a moment's silence, then Sendo answered first, stating that she perceived the Force as balance. Sol approved of this, and the youngling<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Xilawa Dater]]'s<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> answer of "life," then explained that the Force was powerful and must be respected after the student<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Jev Eremia]]<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> answered "[[fire]]." Having seen Jedi Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]] waiting to speak with him, Sol then called the lesson to a close and dismissed Sendo and the others for [[Foodstuff|lunch]]. Opening her eyes and standing, Sendro then bowed to Rwoh before filing out with the other students under the guidance of<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Flurri Wiss]]<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> and another [[Jedi]].<ref name="LostFound" />

==Personality and traits==
As a youngling, Khari Sendo showed early signs of leadership and potential in dispute-settling, encouraging fellow students to open up with their feelings. She had dark skin, [[Color|black]] [[hair]], and brown eyes.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Equipment==
During her lesson with Sol, Sendo wore tan [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] with a brown [[belt]] and brown shoes.<ref name="LostFound" /> The belt's gray buckle bore a seal of the late High Republic.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Khari Sendo was portrayed by [[Sienna Khiroya]] in "[[Lost / Found]],"<ref name="LostFound" /> the first episode of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref> Prior to the release of the episode, she was revealed in a trailer exclusively shown at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="CelebrationDate">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> The scenes in the Jedi Temple were shot at [[Shinfield Studios]],<ref name="Fantha Part I">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Julian Foddy">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=''The Acolyte'' Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy}}</ref> The character was credited only as "youngling" in the episode<ref name="LostFound" /> and she was first named in the [[2025]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

